= Solution
{parent=5}

**False.** Take $\alpha=\beta=1$ and $\gamma=\omega$. Then
$$
(1+1)\omega=2\omega=\omega,
\qquad 1\omega+1\omega=\omega+\omega>\omega.
$$
Thus <ordinal multiplication> on the right does not in general distribute over <ordinal addition>. The side on which <ordinal multiplication> occurs matters; the left-distributive identity in the previous part does not imply this one.

